_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T13:27:29-07:00","id":1228665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1228451-new-night-horrors-book-coming?p=1228624#post1228624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, basically everything I hoped for. A companion book that includes all the antagonists mentioned in the antagonist part of the core book that didn't get full rules. Are the Tremere the only representatives for Liches, or will we get ephemeral Liches too? And will the book introduce a new type of antagonist as well, like many other Night Horror books?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't be surprised if we get a Contagion-related antagonist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T16:44:21-07:00","id":1228705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1228451-new-night-horrors-book-coming?p=1228533#post1228533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And yes, it will have the ... Tremere,</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats a preorder for me!<br /> <br /> Edit: Here is where we are getting the news of this book from:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/waggin-tales-wraithy-wails-monday-meeting-notes/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/waggin-tales-wraithy-wails-monday-meeting-notes/\" target=\"_blank\"> Waggin&rsquo; Tales &amp; Wraithy Wails [Monday Meeting Notes] &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/waggin-tales-wraithy-wails-monday-meeting-notes/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/waggin-tales-wraithy-wails-monday-meeting-notes/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Way down near the bottom in the First Draft section.<ul><li><b>Night Horrors: Nameless and Accursed (Mage: the Awakening Second Edition)</b></li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11799,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","user":"RBAWintrow","date":". 06-19-2018, 07:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","name":"RBAWintrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T16:59:36-07:00","id":1228709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1228451-new-night-horrors-book-coming?p=1228644#post1228644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah thanks. They have a lot of terms for a group the Pentacle tries to lock down and define.</div> </div> </div> </div>Such is the case with pretty much anything that has ties to the Abyss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T11:13:47-07:00","id":1229407,"title":"","content":"Not exactly on topic but what happened to &quot;Tome of the Pentacle&quot;. It was mentioned as the second suplement coming for Mage but there's no info on it in the blurbs. Was it postponed in favor of the Night Horrors book or is being &lt;name part of development process&gt; independently from it ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T11:22:50-07:00","id":1229411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1228451-new-night-horrors-book-coming?p=1229407#post1229407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not exactly on topic but what happened to &quot;Tome of the Pentacle&quot;. It was mentioned as the second suplement coming for Mage but there's no info on it in the blurbs. Was it postponed in favor of the Night Horrors book or is being &lt;name part of development process&gt; independently from it ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I may have read into this wrong, but it appeared to me that Dave is not the main dev for this Night Horrors book which means that this book isn't displacing Tome of the Pentacles which will be the next book Dave is the main dev on once SoS is finished.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T13:40:48-07:00","id":1229446,"title":"","content":"I believe Night Horrors jumped Tome of the Pentacle and Fallen Worlds on the release schedule because much of the book is already written. A great deal of the mage antagonist material needed to be cut for space from the new core, and I expect we'll see most of it in Nameless and Accursed, along with some extra evil goodies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T07:10:04-07:00","id":1229590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1228451-new-night-horrors-book-coming?p=1229446#post1229446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe Night Horrors jumped Tome of the Pentacle and Fallen Worlds on the release schedule because much of the book is already written. A great deal of the mage antagonist material needed to be cut for space from the new core, and I expect we'll see most of it in Nameless and Accursed, along with some extra evil goodies.</div> </div> </div> </div> This makes sense, why let all the work go to waste when it can be repurposed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T05:55:36-07:00","id":1229994,"title":"","content":"As a rule, I have limited interest in antagonist sourcebooks and even less in the horror element of the CoD, so I usually buy Night Horrors books only out of a completist drive, if ever. However, 2e rules for Wisdom 0 and Abyssal mages fill a important hole in the updated system and setting, so I'll give this book a substantially higher priority than its siblings. I care little for the Tremere, but my huge interest for immortal characters makes me very eager for any additional material I can get and use for Liche mages, as long as hopefully the gameline doesn't go out of its way in the infamous Blood Treachery sense to make them unplayable or take a 'bad wrong fun' approach to transhumanist players who have no time or patience for the pro-mortality bias of mage society, except perhaps as a prejudice plot-hook to be defied and circumvented in play. But I'm moderately hopeful this won't happen and Liche PC in practice shall suffer no worse playing penalty than a bad reputation and a taboo against getting political status in Awakened society, the stuff we more or less already know and which I can totally live with.<br /> <br /> On an loosely related note, however, I cannot but notice and lament a much more important and useful book, Signs of Sorcery AKA the de facto player's guide/second half of the corebook's magic system chapter, has been languishing for 26 months in development and counting. Three months ago they told us it was almost done, 93,000-out-of-97,000 words developed, and the last bit was proving tricky. Sadly, I guess the last 4,000 words have been exceptionally tricky, and I'm kind of curious what it is holding back everything else so much. Frankly, this huge delay makes me exceedingly skeptical any MtAw book of any sort is actually going to make real progress in the production pipeline until I see SoS clearing development hell. Although I am seriously interested in Fallen Worlds and to a lesser degree Tome of the Pentacle too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 06-28-2018, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T06:36:39-07:00","id":1230000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1228451-new-night-horrors-book-coming?p=1229994#post1229994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On an loosely related note, however, I cannot but notice and lament a much more important and useful book, Signs of Sorcery AKA the de facto player's guide/second half of the corebook's magic system chapter, has been languishing for 26 months in development and counting. Three months ago they told us it was almost done, 93,000-out-of-97,000 words developed, and the last bit was proving tricky. Sadly, I guess the last 4,000 words have been exceptionally tricky, and I'm kind of curious what it is holding back everything else so much. Frankly, this huge delay makes me exceedingly skeptical any MtAw book of any sort is actually going to make real progress in the production pipeline until I see SoS clearing development hell. Although I am seriously interested in Fallen Worlds and to a lesser degree Tome of the Pentacle too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does every Mage discussion have to devolve into this topic? Shit happens. Is it frustrating? Yes. But we don't know what all of that shit is and as frustrating as it is for us, I would be everything that it's exponentially more frustrating for the writers and developers. Beating the dead horse isn't going help hurry them up.<br /> <br /> Plus, it sounds like this book has a different development team to avoid getting hit by whatever complications are delaying SofS.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T07:01:17-07:00","id":1230004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1228451-new-night-horrors-book-coming?p=1229994#post1229994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I care little for the Tremere, but my huge interest for immortal characters makes me very eager for any additional material I can get and use for Liche mages, as long as hopefully the gameline doesn't go out of its way in the infamous Blood Treachery ghoul-mages sense to make them unplayable or take a 'bad wrong fun' approach on a transhumanist player who has no time or patience for the pro-mortality bias of mage society, except perhaps as a prejudice plot-hook to be defied and circumvented in play. But I'm moderately hopeful this won't happen and Liche PC in practice shall suffer no worse playing penalty than a bad reputation and a taboo against getting political status in Awakened society, the stuff we more or less were already told of in available info and which I can totally live with.</div> </div> </div> </div>This book will most likely focus on Liches as antagonists, but that doesn't in any way preclude Liches as protagonists. In fact, it's only ephemeral Liches that requires any additional rules. If a player wants to play a regular Lich, the tools for longevity through spells or Legacy Attainments are right in the core book. Lich, like Banisher and Reaper, is an in-setting label that can apply both to mages with changed templates but also to regular mages who use their magic in a certain way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T09:05:44-07:00","id":1230026,"title":"","content":"Mages aren't really anti-transhumanist anyway, they're wary of means to remain immortal and Fallen.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso, what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T20:21:03-07:00","id":1230168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1228451-new-night-horrors-book-coming?p=1230004#post1230004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This book will most likely focus on Liches as antagonists, but that doesn't in any way preclude Liches as protagonists. In fact, it's only ephemeral Liches that requires any additional rules. If a player wants to play a regular Lich, the tools for longevity through spells or Legacy Attainments are right in the core book. Lich, like Banisher and Reaper, is an in-setting label that can apply both to mages with changed templates but also to regular mages who use their magic in a certain way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'm under the impression appropriate Legacy Attainments might be kind of necessary to achieve ephemeral Liche status with rules as they stand. However, if they plan to add new rules in this book that would allow to change the template into an ephemeral mage hybrid one without sacrificing the Legacy slot (or access to Supernal magic), I'm all for it, and it would considerably increase the book's appeal and value for me. I'm not enthused about having to tie down the Legacy slot for Liche status when it may be very useful to express other components of the character concept or background that are not related to the quest for immortality. Even more so since in normal circumstances you cannot change your Legacy (nor for that matter get a second one) short of asking an Archmage for an Imperial magic boon (good luck getting one, and Quintessence doesn't exactly grow on trees). On the other hand, as you point out, I'm extremely appreciative of the fact you can effectively be a regular Liche with spells alone. As I said, if things stand for Liche protagonists as indicated from available info, and they are playable short of having a bad reputation and being unable to get political status in Awakened society just as Archmages, I'm satisfied.<br /> <br /> On a side note, the fact never ceases to amuse me since you can't normally change your Legacy one of the best ways to protect yourself from corruption in an Abyssal Legacy is to get a non-Abyssal Legacy you fancy ASAP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 06-27-2018, 03:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T20:34:11-07:00","id":1230170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1228451-new-night-horrors-book-coming?p=1230026#post1230026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages aren't really anti-transhumanist anyway, they're wary of means to remain immortal and Fallen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if you ask my opinion, it is unreasonable to assume each and every mage who is interested in Ascension, or at least becoming an Archmage, should be expected to successfuly complete the quest for it, on top of becoming a sufficiently realized mage to qualify and fit the part, within the span of one measly human life or give up and consign themselves to death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 06-25-2018, 11:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T20:43:34-07:00","id":1230173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1228451-new-night-horrors-book-coming?p=1230170#post1230170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, if you ask my opinion, it is quite unreasonable to assume each and every mage who is interested in Ascension, or at least becoming an Archmage, should be expected to successfuly complete the quest for it,on top of becoming a sufficiently realized mage to qualify and fit the part, within the span of one measly human lifespan or give up and consign themselves to death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you're entitled to your opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T20:45:49-07:00","id":1230175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1228451-new-night-horrors-book-coming?p=1230026#post1230026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages aren't really anti-transhumanist anyway, they're wary of means to remain immortal and Fallen.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso, what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> said.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to burst a bubble in the argument, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=317732#post317732\">except that that's totally what is going to happen here.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T20:47:08-07:00","id":1230176,"title":"","content":"Also, because it wouldn't be fair to only do this Cam:<br /> <br /> Iri.<br /> <br /> Iri.<br /> <br /> Iri.<br /> <br /> <i>We know</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T21:34:51-07:00","id":1230184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1228451-new-night-horrors-book-coming?p=1230175#post1230175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to burst a bubble in the argument, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=317732#post317732\">except that that's totally what is going to happen here.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, some (or many probably) of the Ascended can be antagonists, but Mages don't seem to have an aversion to joining their ranks they way they do with liches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-26T06:08:23-07:00","id":1230254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1228451-new-night-horrors-book-coming?p=1230168#post1230168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On a side note, the fact never ceases to amuse me since you can't normally change your Legacy one of the best ways to protect yourself from corruption in an Abyssal Legacy is to get a non-Abyssal Legacy you fancy ASAP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... *scribbles stuff in homebrew notes.<br /> <br /> If the book has Nameless Orders' mages in general, I wonder if we'd get info on some of the less antagonistic Nameless (who can still be antagonists to the greater sects), like the Elemental Masteries. Maybe even the Vidanti - IIRC, they're now designed as a Nameless Order within the Arrow, yes? (I still want the Tremere. I need to stat up the Flayer.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T18:30:48-07:00","id":1230711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1228451-new-night-horrors-book-coming?p=1228533#post1228533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yes, it will have the 2e <b>Scelesti</b>, Mad One*, <b>Tremere</b>, Integrity-not-Wisdom Banishers, etc rules in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is amazing news.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T22:24:58-07:00","id":1232313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1228451-new-night-horrors-book-coming?p=1230184#post1230184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, some (or many probably) of the Ascended can be antagonists, but Mages don't seem to have an aversion to joining their ranks they way they do with liches.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which makes total and utter sense.<br /> <br /> Because the Ascended don't <i>eat people </i>if they don't want to be ephemeral beings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T23:08:40-07:00","id":1232317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1228451-new-night-horrors-book-coming?p=1232313#post1232313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which makes total and utter sense.<br /> <br /> Because the Ascended don't <i>eat people </i>if they don't want to be ephemeral beings.</div> </div> </div> </div>...<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> ..have you <i>met</i> the Ascended?<br /> <br /> I would not put anything past any of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T02:17:39-07:00","id":1232334,"title":"","content":"Also, Liches don't necessarily want to eat people. You're probably referring to a very specific type of Lich (the Tremere who consume souls, perhaps?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T07:28:31-07:00","id":1232365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1228451-new-night-horrors-book-coming?p=1232334#post1232334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Liches don't necessarily want to eat people. You're probably referring to a very specific type of Lich (the Tremere who consume souls, perhaps?).</div> </div> </div> </div>Problem is, it's explicitly said you change yourself into a form that can't die of old age...or you steal that life from others.<br /> <br /> I consider that people eating, even if it's more abstract than that-you consume other lives to support your own.<br /> <br /> Good point on the Ascended, but, and this is a large but, it's not obligatory for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T10:47:30-07:00","id":1233221,"title":"","content":"I don't think a simple anti aging spell would really be considered a Lich, biological immortality is found in the natural world among rare species and you can still die from countless other causes and your still biologically human. <br /> <br /> Still I agree that I don't buy Mage as an to tranahumanism either, it can't be antitranshuman, because Mages have already transcended regular human abilities, vastly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T11:48:23-07:00","id":1233235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1228451-new-night-horrors-book-coming?p=1233221#post1233221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think a simple anti aging spell would really be considered a Lich, biological immortality is found in the natural world among rare species and you can still die from countless other causes and your still biologically human.<br /> <br /> Still I agree that I don't buy Mage as an to tranahumanism either, it can't be antitranshuman, because Mages have already transcended regular human abilities, vastly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Games are up to personal interpretation, of course, and if it's not how you see it, cool.<br /> <br /> But it should be noted, as accounting go, that Dave has gone on record <i>an awful lot</i> that he does not consider Awakening to be a transhumanist game. Make of that what you will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T13:15:48-07:00","id":1233253,"title":"","content":"It's certainly true that Mages who don't concern themselves with humanity are the ones most likely to go off the rails.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T13:31:44-07:00","id":1233255,"title":"","content":"The Night Horrors line has been consistently good, even the curveballs like Wicked Dead. I imagine everyone's going to find something they really like in it, even folks who don't run mage will likely have shiny new antagonists to put into play with second edition rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T01:39:43-07:00","id":1251312,"title":"","content":"Book is now off to Redlines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T02:09:37-07:00","id":1251314,"title":"","content":"As for the transhumanist discussion: I always found Mage a very humanist game, cause with all the power that the Awakened have the struggles and temptations they face are awfully human in mature. That's also why i like the Seers as an antagonist, they're PAINFULLY human.<br /> <br /> Also feeling the urge to rant about why I don't like the term &quot;tranhumanism&quot; but that's not the place for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-05T04:43:57-07:00","id":1251617,"title":"","content":"mages aren't anti-transhumanist. <b>Mage</b> is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-05T05:11:49-07:00","id":1251623,"title":"","content":"I'd argue the transhumanist game is Demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-05T05:37:38-07:00","id":1251632,"title":"","content":"Hasn't it been said mage is about not about teanshumanism, but simply being more of what makes humans great","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-05T06:03:41-07:00","id":1251635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1228451-new-night-horrors-book-coming?p=1251632#post1251632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hasn't it been said mage is about not about teanshumanism, but simply being more of what makes humans great</div> </div> </div> </div>Who knows? People are throwing it around like there's a single definition when there clearly isn't. Or probably more accurately, it has different implications for different people.<br /> <br /> I mean, Irioth clearly meant it in a fairly limited sense. They wanted a way for a character to live a very long time without needing to start sacrificing people. Is that transhumanism or just letting a person be human for longer?<br /> <br /> Is a mage a 'transhuman'?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-05T07:02:40-07:00","id":1251653,"title":"","content":"Mage is about how true spiritual enlightenment may yield real insights about the self and the world, but doesn't necessarily have a positive effect on one's morality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":61,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","user":"Octavo","date":". 09-05-2018, 10:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-05T12:17:15-07:00","id":1251737,"title":"","content":"Like all the CoD games, Mage has strong elements of horror at its core. Most forms of transhumanism don't really mesh well with horror -- they're too optimistic. Transhumanist thought tends to be based on the idea that it's possible to become superhuman without losing anything valuable in the process. Horror stories in general don't tend to share this assumption; the kind of horror most CoD games specialize in is specifically about trying to remain morally human, or at least humane, in circumstances that threaten your humanity. If existence as a supernatural being <i>doesn't</i> threaten your humanity in some way, then there's no central conflict. Demon is something of an exception in that the Unchained were never human and never will be, but there's still an implication that humanity is valuable and worth protecting from the God-Machine's depredations. (Beast is also kind of an exception, but that's more down to inconsistent writing than anything else.<br /> <br /> If you're looking for a game that's fundamentally optimistic about humanity's potential to exceed its limitations, I recommend Aeon. The CoD games, however, take it as axiomatic that you can't get something for nothing. (I don't mean that in a judgmental way; I have transhumanist sympathies myself. But CoD is not about transhumanism.)<br /> <br /> EDIT: On further reflection, it occurs to me that Geist has some thematic resonance with transhumanism; Sin-Eaters aren't trying to <i>eliminate</i> death as such, but they're trying to make what comes <i>after</i> death less harsh and unfair. If the afterlife is verifiably real, achieving literal immortality is less important than ensuring that you have a nice place to &quot;retire&quot; to. If ghosts are still people, and if the oppressive systems that govern the Underworld can be changed, then what is there to fear in death?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":40,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/40-dspaul","user":"DSPaul","date":". 09-05-2018, 03:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/40-dspaul","name":"DSPaul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-05T15:56:54-07:00","id":1251781,"title":"","content":"I reread an great story by Thomas Ligotti recently called Masquerade of a Dead Sword that had an interesting depiction of the Awakening, without the magical ability attached to it and the maddening nihilism that could lead from such an experience. Complete with an appearance from the Anima Mundi.<br /> <br /> 'Reality is a prison designed by tyranny and there's no reliable way out' isn't exactly a transhumanist perspective.<br /> <br /> But you can still be a transhumanist mage, and some of the lines have transhumanist factions, like the Ordo Dracul and Ivory Claws, though that verges on transmonsterism. Still have Cheiron and whatever TFV is willing to do to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-05-2018, 07:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-24T11:09:50-08:00","id":1276497,"title":"","content":"Book's off to Development.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}